{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: client and deployment hygiene (simplification review 55563589, findings SEC-04, SEC-05, SEC-11). (1) PUBLIC_URL falls back to https://artroom.example.workers.dev (packages/room/src/room.ts:79) and packages/room/wrangler.jsonc:31 sets that placeholder; the CLI then prints a claude mcp add command sending the bearer token to that host. Make PUBLIC_URL required with no fallback, fail at startup without it, and remove the placeholder. (2) The CLI writes the server-supplied remote and token verbatim into a git config include (packages/cli/src/git.ts:61); quotes or newlines inject config keys that run code on the next git command. Validate remote as a strict https URL and token against a strict character class, and write the config through git config arguments, not string templating. (3) Bodies are read whole before the 1 MiB check when there is no Content-Length (room/src/http.ts:47-51), and the MCP route has no cap (mcp/src/worker.ts:45-52). Count bytes while streaming and abort past the cap on both.","body":{"conditions":"Each item with a test that failed before the fix; the room refuses to start without PUBLIC_URL; the CLI refuses a grant with a malformed remote or token; root gates pass; checker review.","target_head":"a6330262b1a609843308d9a493dbd6132d428499","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}